Chapter: IdentitySetprocNoAdmin

 A process that drops capability-admin cannot write a process's
 identity through identity-set-proc, even its own and even though it
 still holds the identity bit: identity-set-proc tests both bits.
 The child targets its own pid, so the denial is exercised without a
 second process (see identity-cap-gate for the cross-process path).

Section: Body
  child-set : Integer -> [Identity, Capability] Integer
  child-set (r) = poke-byte 28000 0 (if identity-set-proc (process-get-pid) 0 888 == (0 - 1) then 1 else 0)

  child-body : Integer -> [Capability, Identity] Integer
  child-body (x) = child-set (process-restrict-cap (process-get-pid) 14)

  verdict : Integer -> Text
  verdict (child) =
    let wt = process-wait child
    in if peek-byte 28000 0 == 1 then "PASS: identity-set-proc denied without cap-admin"
    else "FAIL"

  opening : [Console, Concurrent, Capability, Identity] Nothing = act
    child <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    print-line-uni (verdict child)
  end
